# The Physics sheet — AI-course sims

The product, voice and quality bar are the uni-lab Physics sheet's
(`.cursor/rules/physics-sheet-upgrade.mdc`); the AI-course kit and its differences are
in `.cursor/skills/physics-sheet-upgrade/ai-courses/` (`<kit>/` below).
**Read `<kit>/README.md` first**, then `.cursor/skills/physics-sheet-upgrade/references/content.md`
and `references/pitfalls.md`. They are the specification.

## Non-negotiables

- **Only the marker changes.** Every AI sim is pre-wired (the button, its listener,
  `window.__physicsHooks.scene`, the fonts). Do NOT apply the uni-lab skill's four
  structural patches. `assemble_ai.py` replaces `<!-- PHYSICS_SHEET -->` with the layer and
  proves the rest of the file is byte-identical — never bypass it, never hand-edit the sim.
- **Physics from the course notes.** Each sim's sections are in `<kit>/notes_anchors.json`;
  the PDF is in the course folder. Use the notes' symbols and the sim's on-screen labels;
  **never change or introduce a symbol without SME sign-off**. If the notes, the sim and
  the Guided Inquiry disagree, or a physics claim looks wrong, **stop and report it** —
  do not "fix" the sim and do not paper over it in the sheet.
- **Every number recomputed** from the sim's own code (and checked against its readout in
  the browser); figures computed from the sim's defaults, never sketched.
- **Guided Inquiry stays intact**: the layer pauses See-its while the cards are on screen —
  keep that machinery verbatim. The kicker names the topic, never the answer.
- **Seven question-led chapters**, live ch 03 bound to the sim's real controls, worked run
  from current values, 3 TikZ figures, See-its that pass current values (the scene resets
  controls to defaults first).

## Steps (per sim — details in `<kit>/README.md`)

1. Recon: shell family (kit vs legacy), controls, `scene()` keys, readouts, Info modal,
   GI cards, notes sections.
2. Author in a scratch dir outside the repo: `spec.py` → `../scripts/gen_assets.py` → look at
   every PNG; `article.html`; `persim.js` (`MINI`, `LIVE`, `SHOW`); `meta.json`.
3. `python3 <kit>/assemble_ai.py <sim> <work>` (dry) → `node <kit>/browser_test_ai.mjs <work>/built.html <work>/shots`
   must print `RESULT PASS`; look at every screenshot.
4. `assemble_ai.py <sim> <work> --apply`, re-run the browser gate on the real file, then
   `node <kit>/gi_reset_test.mjs <listfile> 4` → `FAIL 0`.
5. Report: numbers checked, screenshots viewed, anything held for the SME.

Never commit the scratch work dirs, screenshots or notes text.
